timeline.body:
@jimczi & @javanna take a look at my comments. This was difficult to nail down, but it has to do with us wrapping leaf readers and then using sub-readers instead of the top level reader when calculating weights for highlighting.

Its weird, since this is the path for `weight_offsets`, for highlighting to occur, it HAS to be matched by some other query, the knn query has no baring on the highlighting at all in this context. It just might have boosted the score. 

I wonder if we could some how bypass the `knn` weight? Or swallow the failure somehow and just skip using its weight?
